From c228e570733d71bffde1485754e58d11269a31da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mikkojhuttunen <mikkojhuttunen@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 17:50:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Cavity workbench: gain-free DHW starting cavities with
 spec-only names
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The DHW1 and DHW2 starting cavities no longer contain a gain medium, so
students choose and insert it themselves. The pump arm is the design
arm minus the 10 mm crystal (240 mm and 104 mm), which keeps both empty
cavities stable and restores the design length once a crystal is added.
The example names now give only the specification, e.g. "DHW1:
1064.2 nm, linewidth ≈ 1 MHz, > 5 W output", and the linear demo no
longer names its crystal.

Adding the first gain crystal now places it in the middle of the arm
behind the pump-window mirror, splitting that gap in two, instead of
appending it at the end of the ring.

Both editions regenerated; the student file still matches the pro
master after the PRO-ONLY blocks are stripped.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015k2UYA58Ace5jVaSrfKnkj
